# AI workflow

Task size:
- One task card = one chat session = one branch, one commit, one PR. Target 30–90 minutes of work.
- A task card has: Spec link, Files, Do, Don't, Done when (see `docs/tasks/_template.md`).
- If a task grows beyond its card, stop and propose splitting it.

Context hygiene:
- Reference exact files (`@path`) instead of scanning the whole repo.
- Specs, ADRs, and feature docs are the memory. Chat history is not.
- One source of truth: each rule or fact lives in one file (see the "Where things go" table in `AGENTS.md`). Elsewhere, link to it instead of restating it.
- When you find a duplicate, keep the copy in the right place and replace the others with a link. `docs/progress.md` and ADRs are snapshots and may restate.
- Before ending a session, use the `handoff` skill to update `docs/progress.md`.
- If the session repeats mistakes or contradicts earlier decisions, recommend starting a fresh chat.

Decisions:
- Any choice that is hard to reverse (store, library, auth model, data shape) gets an ADR.
